<p>North Korea said it “respects” and supports Iran’s selection of Mojtaba Khamenei as the country’s new supreme leader, according to statements carried by its state media and reported by multiple outlets. The comments followed Iranian media reports that Mojtaba Khamenei had been selected as supreme leader. Pyongyang also condemned the U.S. and Israel for what it called an unlawful or illegal military attack against Iran, arguing that the strikes erode regional peace and add to broader global instability.</p><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>State media channel: A North Korean Foreign Ministry spokesperson made the remarks, which the KCNA state news agency carried, according to Reuters-reported coverage.</li><li>Peace framing: North Korea said the strikes “are destroying peace” and fueling instability worldwide, casting its position as a defense of global stability.</li><li>Regional stability: North Korea accused the U.S. and Israel of undercutting regional peace in connection with the attack on Iran.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>North Korean Foreign Ministry (via KCNA): North Korea said it supports the Iranian people’s choice of Mojtaba Khamenei and denounced U.S. and Israeli attacks on Iran as “illegal,” saying they destroy peace and deepen global instability. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/north-korea-supports-irans-choice-new-supreme-leader-kcna-says'>Al-Monitor (via Reuters)</a>)</li><li>Al Jazeera reporting: Al Jazeera described North Korea’s message as respect for Iran’s selection of Mojtaba Khamenei, while highlighting Pyongyang’s condemnation of what it called an “unlawful military attack against Iran”. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/11/n-korea-respects-irans-selection-of-mojtaba-khamenei-as-supreme-leader'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>NDTV reporting: NDTV highlighted North Korea’s claim that U.S. and Israeli actions undermine regional peace, alongside Pyongyang’s statement that it “respects” Iran’s choice of supreme 